{
  "description": "Phoneme tags say what a token sounds like, and phonemes() of later stages reads them (engine §5).",
  "documents": {
    "p.md": "## s <?stage sounds?>\n\n- [g](g.md) <?grammar?>\n\n## t <?stage words?>\n\n- [h](h.md) <?grammar?>\n",
    "g.md": "```ebnf\n%ambiguity-resolution greedy ;\ntext ≔ [c] ... ;\nc ≔ \"a\" </a/> | \"Á\" </A/> | \"space\" </ /> ⇒ this ;\n```\n",
    "h.md": "```ebnf\n%ambiguity-resolution greedy ;\ntext ≔ $w(pair) : phonemes($w) = \"aA\" ;\npair ≔ /a/ /A/ ;\n```\n"
  },
  "pipeline": "p.md",
  "input": "aÁ",
  "expect": {
    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stages": [
        {
          "output": [
            {
              "text": "a",
              "phonemes": "a"
            },
            {
              "text": "Á",
              "phonemes": "A"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "verdict": "unique"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
